,title,link,text,language,family
0,Kuki-Chin languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuki-Chin_languages,"The Kuki-Chin languages (also called Kukish[2] or South-Central Tibeto-Burman languages) are a branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family spoken in northeastern India, western Myanmar and southeastern Bangladesh.Sate/Awsa. Senthang. Khuapi. Surkhua.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
1,Senthang Chin - sez (Sino-Tibetan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/sez/,"Senthang Chin (sez) is part of the Sino-Tibetan family and Sino-Tibetan, Tibeto-Burman, Kuki-Chin, Maraic class.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
2,"Chin, Senthang Language (SEZ)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/sez/,Senthang Chin is a stable indigenous language of Myanmar. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family.,"Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
3,Senthang language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/senthang_language,"The Senthang language, also known as Senthang Chin (ISO 639-3: sez), is a Sino-Tibetan language of the Tibeto-Burman branch, specifically within the Kuki-Chin subgroup, spoken primarily by the Senthan.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
4,Sino-Tibetan,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Sino-Tibetan.htm,"The Sino-Tibetan Language Phylum. SiniticMaraic: i. Senthang Chin, Zotung Chin, Zyphe Chin ii. Mara: Lautu Chin, Mara Chin. Northwestern Kuki-Chin: Aimol, Anal, Chiru, Kom, Lamkang, Chothe Naga, Kharam Naga, Monsang Naga, Tarao Naga.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
5,Senthang Chin Translation Services | Language Guide | LEXIGO,https://lexigo.com/languages/senthang-chin,"Senthang (also known as Senthang Chin) is a Kuki-Chin language of the Sino-Tibetan family spoken by approximately 15,000 people, primarily in southern Chin State, Myanmar.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
6,"Chin, Senthang in Myanmar (Burma) people group... | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/14857/BM,"The Senthang Chin are a Tibeto-Himalayan group of people, a sub-family of the Chin-Hakha-Lai race. In accordance with the genealogy of Senthang, Pu Mang Sui founded the senthang clan.","Chin, Senthang",Sino-Tibetan
